   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT in relation to permitting Patchogue Fire District to file an\napplication for a retroactive real property tax exemption",
    "basePrintNo": "S6585",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6585-2019",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Real Property Taxation",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S6585\n\nSPONSOR: MARTINEZ\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act in relation to permitting Patchogue Fire\nDistrict to file an application for a retroactive real property tax\nexemption\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA:\n\nTo authorize the assessor of the Town of Brookhaven to accept from the\nPatchogue Fire District, application for exemption from real property\ntaxes from 2016-2017 and 2017-2018 assessment rolls.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nAuthorizes the assessor of the town of Brookhaven, Suffolk County, to\naccept an application for a real property tax exemption under section\n406 of the Real Property Tax Law from the Patchogue Fire District for\nthe parcels located at 29 Jennings Avenue in Patchogue, NY, also known\nas district 0204, section 009.00, block 02.00, lot 012.000 and at 25\nPark Street in Patchogue, NY, also known as, district 0204, section\n017.00, block 4.00, lot 024.000 and at a vacant lot on Park Street in\nPatchogue, NY, also known as, district 0204, section 017.00, block 4.00,\nlot 025.000 in the Town of Brookhaven, county of Suffolk for the\n2016-2017 and 2017-2018 tax rolls. Upon satisfaction that the organiza-\ntion would have otherwise been entitled to said exemption, but for an\nadministrative error, the assessor may grant this exemption upon\napproval of the town board. Further, the town board, at its sole\ndiscretion, may provide for the refund of taxes paid and cancel taxes,\nfines, penalties, liens, or interest remaining unpaid.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis bill authorizes a retroactive tax exemption to a legally recognized\ntax exempt organization by notwithstanding the exemption application\ndeadline for two assessment rolls so the municipality may submit such\napplication for exemption.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nA.10148 of 2018: Passed Assembly 135-1. Died in Senate Rules Committee.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to the State. Negligible to the municipality.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediate.\n",
